<title>HONG KONG: China's forex reserves hit US$110 bln - PBOC.</title>
<headline>China's forex reserves hit US$110 bln - PBOC.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's foreign exchange reserves amounted to US$110 billion at the end of February, the Governor of the People's Bank of China Dai Xianglong said in Hong Kong on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;At the end of this February, China's foreign exchange reserves amounted to US$110 billion,&quot; Dai told an International Monetary Fund (IMF)-Hong Kong Monetary Authority conference in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>The People's Bank serves as China's central bank.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6352</p>
